 "section_summary": "This section contains Embassy Report No. 1677 for July 1941 and a duplicate copy transmitted under Despatch No. 5812 by Ambassador Joseph C. Grew. The documents detail the Japanese military occupation of southern French Indochina and the subsequent retaliatory freezing of Japanese assets by the United States, Great Britain, and the Netherlands East Indies. They also report on the Japanese bombing of the USS Tutuila at Chungking, the collapse of the Second Konoye Cabinet and ouster of Foreign Minister Matsuoka, and escalating Japanese military mobilizations facing Manchuria.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "Continuation of Embassy Report No. 1677 covering political, diplomatic, military, and economic developments in Japan during July 1941.",
