   ],
   "start_page": 461,
   "summary": "Ambassador Joseph C. Grew transmits to the Secretary of State a duplicate copy of Embassy Report No. 1677 reviewing developments in Japan during July 1941. The included portion contains the transmittal letter, report index, complete lists of telegrams and despatches sent to the Department during July, and narrative sections on Japanese-American and Anglo-Japanese relations. Topics include the Vichy-Japanese joint defense accord over French Indochina, American and British retaliatory asset freezes, the near-sinking of the USS Tutuila at Chungking, and British denunciation of commercial treaties with Japan.",
   "title": "Despatch No. 5812 Transmitting Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of July 1941 (Report No. 1677, Duplicate Copy)",
   "to": "The Secretary of State"
  }
 ],
